card.statement:
The following conditions are equivalent for an element $\Lambda$ of a reductive Lie algebra $\mf g$:

[(i)]

- $\ad\Lambda$ is a semisimple endomorphism of $\mf g$;

- the adjoint orbit of $\Lambda$ is closed;

- $\ker(\ad\Lambda)\cap\im(\ad\Lambda)=0$;

- $\mf g=\ker(\ad\Lambda)+\im(\ad\Lambda)$;

- $\mf g=\ker(\ad\Lambda)\oplus\im(\ad\Lambda)$.
